        <body>
            <div xml:id="d225">

                <pb facs="0295" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">J. C. S. Files</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Joint Chiefs of Staff to the President</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Aboard the</hi> U. S. S. “<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Iowa</hi>”</placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-17"
                            >17 November 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for the
                    President</hi>:</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Command of British and U. S. Forces Operating Against
                    Germany.</p>
                <p>The Joint Chiefs of Staff present herewith for your consideration drafts of two
                    proposals, Enclosure “A” and Enclosure “B”, relative to the command arrangements
                    for the European Theater.</p>
                <p>It is the opinion of the Joint Chiefs of Staff that Enclosure “A” is the more
                    sound and from a military point of view is the better plan.</p>
                <closer>For the Joint Chiefs of Staff:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >William D. Leahy</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Admiral, U.
                        S. Navy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chief of Staff to the Commander in
                        Chief of the Army and Navy</hi></closer>







